operations.para:
	The name is checked as you type. While it can't be used, the Save button is disabled and a message under the field says why. A name can't be used if it
	

is empty;

contains line breaks, tabs, or other invisible characters;

contains < or >;

starts or ends with a space;

is too long to store (255 characters, where a ' counts as 6 and accented letters as 2 or more);

exactly matches (including capitalization) the name of one of your own models of the same type.
	 When the name is new, Save (or Enter) saves the model in the VCell database.
	Cancel (or Esc) cancels the save operation.
